    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:userTask id="sign-in" name="Signs up or signs in">
      <bpmn:documentation>A username of 3 to 24 letters, numbers, dots, dashes or underscores, in any alphabet, and a password — or Google, which makes the account at once under a drawn name like kringel-4821, changed later on the account page. Inside Instagram, Facebook or TikTok, Google is offered from the phone's own browser instead. No email. The iPhone app offers the same two and Apple, which makes its account the way Google does.
when: account_create
when: account_login
ref: index.html the account sheet
ref: assets/app.js</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>visitor-e18</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>visitor-e25</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>visitor-e30</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>visitor-e31</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>visitor-e32</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="session" name="Opens a session, claims this device's saves">
      <bpmn:documentation>Then back to the page that asked, over the map. From Save on a list, that list is kept on arrival.
ref: functions/api/account.js POST create, login, ticket
ref: functions/api/_account.js claimDeviceSaves(), makeGoogleAccount()
ref: functions/api/google.js GET
ref: functions/api/apple.js POST
ref: assets/lists.js keepAsked()</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>visitor-e32</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>visitor-e33</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
